# 🔌 API Overview

## AI Routes

Base route:

```http
/api/ai
```

Main operations include:

```http
POST /write-article
POST /generate-titles
POST /generate-image
POST /remove-background
POST /remove-object
POST /review-resume
```

These routes are responsible for the application's AI functionality.

---

## User Routes

Base route:

```http
/api/users
```

User-related functionality includes:

```http
GET  /profile
GET  /creations
POST /creations
GET  /community
```

Protected routes use authentication middleware to verify the current user.

---

# 🔐 Authentication Flow

```text
User Login
    ↓
Clerk
    ↓
Authentication Token
    ↓
Frontend API Request
    ↓
Express Auth Middleware
    ↓
Verify User
    ↓
Controller
    ↓
Protected Resource
```

This prevents unauthenticated users from accessing protected AI functionality.

---

# 🗄️ Database

The project uses **PostgreSQL hosted on Neon**.

The database stores information such as:

- User-related creation data
- AI-generated content
- Generated image URLs
- Creation metadata
- Public/private creation status

The application communicates with PostgreSQL through the backend rather than directly from the React frontend.

---

# ⚙️ Getting Started

## Prerequisites

Make sure you have:

```text
Node.js 18+
npm
Neon PostgreSQL account
Clerk account
Cloudinary account
OpenAI API credentials
```

---

## 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Pawankumar1188/QuickAiFrontend.git
cd QuickAiFrontend
```

---

## 2. Install Frontend Dependencies

```bash
cd client
npm install
```

---

## 3. Install Backend Dependencies

Open another terminal:

```bash
cd server
npm install
```

---

# 🔑 Environment Variables

Never commit your real `.env` files or API keys to GitHub.

## Client

Create:

```text
client/.env
```

Add:

```env
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your_clerk_publishable_key
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000
```

---

## Server

Create:

```text
server/.env
```

Add:

```env
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key

CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your_cloudinary_cloud_name
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=your_cloudinary_api_key
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=your_cloudinary_api_secret

DATABASE_URL=your_neon_postgresql_connection_string

CLERK_SECRET_KEY=your_clerk_secret_key

PORT=5000
```

---

# ▶️ Run Locally

## Start Backend

```bash
cd server
npm run server
```

The backend will run on:

```text
http://localhost:5000
```

---

## Start Frontend

Open another terminal:

```bash
cd client
npm run dev
```

Vite will provide a development URL such as:

```text
http://localhost:5173
```

---

# 🚀 Deployment

## Frontend

The Nexora.AI frontend is deployed using **Netlify**.

Live application:

### https://nexona-ai.netlify.app/

Production environment variables should be configured through the Netlify dashboard rather than committed to GitHub.

---

## Database

The PostgreSQL database is hosted using **Neon Serverless PostgreSQL**.

```text
Application
    ↓
Express Backend
    ↓
Neon PostgreSQL
```

---

## Media Storage

Uploaded and processed images are handled using **Cloudinary**.

Cloudinary provides:

- Cloud image storage
- CDN delivery
- Background removal
- Generative object removal
- Image transformations

---

# 🔒 Security

The application follows several basic security practices:

- Authentication using Clerk
- Protected backend routes
- Environment variables for API credentials
- Server-side database access
- Controlled file uploads using Multer
- CORS configuration
- Cloud-based image storage instead of storing uploads permanently on the application server

> API keys and database credentials should never be committed to the repository.

